<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20460] lctl set_param -P silently fails to register sptlrpc flavor rules</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20460</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;`lctl set_param -P &amp;lt;fs&amp;gt;.srpc.flavor.X=Y` returns success but does not register an sptlrpc rule. The parameter is errorneously put into the generic params log as an LCFG_SET_PARAM record instead of the per-filesystem &amp;lt;fs&amp;gt;-sptlrpc log as an LCFG_SPTLRPC_CONF record, so the MGS never enforces it or transmits it to clients.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The equivalent lctl conf_param works and is de-facto the expected way to configure persistent sptlrpc rules today.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This bug has been noticed multiple times in the past, it appears to have been originally reported in: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-7183" title="lctl set_param -P does not work for sptlrpc flavor" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-7183"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-7183&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, which was closed as duplicate by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10937" title="Use sysfs to fix up sptlrpc handling so set_param works" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10937"&gt;LU-10937&lt;/a&gt;. However &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10937" title="Use sysfs to fix up sptlrpc handling so set_param works" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10937"&gt;LU-10937&lt;/a&gt; has a much broader intent, including a migration towards sysfs, while the original set_param -P gap remains unfixed still.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Example%3A"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Example:&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;set_param -P&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
[root@server1 ~]# lctl set_param -P lustre.srpc.flavor.tcp103=&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;
[root@server1 ~]# lctl get_param mgs.MGS.live.lustre | grep tcp103 
# Nothing, rule is not applied
[root@server1 ~]# lctl llog_print lustre-sptlrpc | grep tcp103
# Nothing
[root@server1 ~]# lctl --device MGS llog_print params | grep tcp103
- { index: 54, event: set_param, device: general, parameter: lustre.srpc.flavor.tcp103, value: &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; }
# Entry placed into the params log mistakenly
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;conf_param&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
[root@server1 ~]# lctl conf_param lustre.srpc.flavor.tcp103=&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;
[root@server1 ~]# lctl get_param mgs.MGS.live.lustre | grep tcp103
lustre.srpc.flavor.tcp103=&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;
# Rule is active
[root@server1 ~]# lctl llog_print lustre-sptlrpc | grep tcp103
- { index: 360, event: security, device: lustre, parameter: srpc.flavor.tcp103=&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; }
# Rule place into &amp;lt;fs&amp;gt;-sptlrpc log
[root@server1 ~]# lctl --device MGS llog_print params | grep tcp103 
# params log empty as expected
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It would be good to fix this behaviour so that we can fully deprecate conf_param for usage in this area.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
